==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|matr||food|lang=non}} from the {{proto|Germanic|matiz|lang=fo}}. Whence also Old English {{term|mete|mēte|lang=ang}} (Middle English {{term|mete|mēte|lang=enm}} from which English {{term|meat|lang=en}} came); Gothic {{term|mats}}; Old High German {{term|maz}}, Swedish {{term|mat|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|mad|lang=da}} and Icelandic {{term|matur|lang=is}}.

